KNOWN GAP, owned by `make-a-posix-target-is-read-where-it-is-written`.

The statement is evaluated after the file it stands in has been read whole, so
the flag it sets cannot reach a fold above it in that file. The evaluator sets
the flag for whatever is read after the eval, which is what makes an eval above
a LATER include work.

GNU Make 4.4.1 keeps the blanks in front of the fold and writes `[a    b]`;
Ronin writes `[a b]`.
